skills.card:
aspectRatio — Reduce a width by a height to its screen ratio, like 16:9.
  needs: width: number, height: number
  e.g. "what aspect ratio is 1920 by 1080" → {"width":1920,"height":1080}

complementaryColor — Find the colour opposite a given one on the colour wheel.
  needs: color: string
  e.g. "what is the complement of #2C6E8C" → {"color":"#2C6E8C"}

convertColor — Convert a colour between hex, RGB and HSL.
  needs: color: string
  e.g. "convert #FF5733 to rgb" → {"color":"#FF5733"}

nearestNamedColor — Find the closest CSS colour name to a colour — what you would call it in words.
  needs: color: string
  e.g. "what colour name is closest to #556B2F" → {"color":"#556B2F"}

correlation — Measure how strongly two sets of numbers move together, as a correlation coefficient.
  needs: x: array, y: array
  e.g. "how correlated are these two series" → {"x":[1,2,3,4,5],"y":[2,4,6,8,10]}

percentile — Find the value at a given percentile in a set of numbers.
  needs: values: array, percentile: number
  e.g. "what is the 90th percentile of these response times" → {"values":[12,15,18,22,30,45,60,90,120,300],"percentile":90}

quartiles — Split a set of numbers into quartiles and give the interquartile range.
  needs: values: array
  e.g. "quartiles of 1 through 8" → {"values":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8]}

weightedAverage — Average a set of values where some count for more than others.
  needs: values: array, weights: array
  e.g. "weighted average of 80 and 90 where the second counts double" → {"values":[80,90],"weights":[1,2]}

fileExtensionInfo — Say what kind of file an extension is and which media type it uses.
  needs: query: string
  e.g. "what kind of file is .csv" → {"query":".csv"}

textFileStats — Count the lines, words and bytes in a piece of text and describe its line endings.
  needs: text: string
  e.g. "stats for this text" → {"text":"hello world"}

